# Cursor Working Rule

Before coding:
- read relevant approved specs;
- identify affected rule/domain boundary.

After coding, report:
1. What changed.
2. Which approved requirement it implements.
3. Tests added/updated.
4. Any unresolved decision discovered.
5. Any migration/config action required.

Stop and ask instead of guessing when:
- product behavior is undefined;
- economy value is undefined;
- real-money price is needed;
- canon would change;
- cloud choice adds meaningful recurring cost;
- Solver change alters gameplay rules;
- migration risks player data.
